<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Limpopo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Limpopo is a major river of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, flowing through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. It marks the southern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwe plateau</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-zimbabwe">Great Zimbabwe</a> and its successor states developed. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a> place the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> and the Limpopo at the centre of its world.</p></div>
